would leave the suite green while the assertion is inert"],"finding":"The 'load-bearing' check — seed a ticket into the template, confirm fixture raises, then remove the seed — is explicitly described as a 'temporary local check' and never becomes a durable AC or CI artifact. No ongoing enforcement proves the new assertion actually catches a pre-seeded template; the green suite only proves no false positive.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb4f9a63c01f702c1","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing section; Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n23fbe03371d586d7","priority":0.4125,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["Executor writes `assert len(rebar.list_tickets()) == 0` but mistakenly passes the wrong repo path; assertion always passes vacuously; tier is green; the invariant is unenforced; the completion verifier cannot distinguish this from a correct implementation."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add an AC: 'Temporarily seeding a ticket into the template immediately after `rebar.init_repo()` and re-running the fixture causes it to raise `AssertionError` (or equivalent); removing the seed restores a green run. The executor records this output as evidence on the ticket.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","vague/subjective terms present: properly"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a proving command (e.g. `grep -n 'list_tickets' tests/interfaces/conftest.py` plus a comment or structural note) or a dedicated AC that verifies the assertion appears inside the `MonkeyPatch.context()` block, not only that the suite passes.","cohort":["E2","E6","F1"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'asserts the freshly built template has no tickets, inside the MonkeyPatch context where REBAR_ROOT and cwd are pinned'","'The durable evidence is the tier passing with the assertion in place'","pytest passing does not prove the assertion is inside vs. outside the context block — both placements produce a green suite when the template is clean"],"finding":"AC1 requires the assertion to be placed INSIDE the MonkeyPatch context block, but the only proving command (`pytest tests/interfaces -q`) cannot distinguish a correctly placed assertion from one placed outside the context (both would pass when the template is clean). There is no grep/structural check that verifies the placement constraint.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4a37034b8221fc49","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — first bullet; Testing section","norm_id":"ndc43e3ac83798565","priority":0.3438,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["An executor places the assertion after the `with` block exits; the suite passes because the template is clean; the placement invariant (REBAR_ROOT/cwd pinned) is silently violated; a future reader or refactor moves it further without noticing."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add an AC: 'A `grep` or AST check confirms the `list_tickets` assertion appears between the `monkeypatch.context()` entry and its exit (i.e., before the `with` block closes).' Alternatively, embed a small comment marker (`# INSIDE_MONKEYPATCH_CONTEXT`) and grep for it alongside the assertion.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v4","material_fingerprint":"8f3fd86c959f9939","metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":81396,"cache_write_tokens":15570,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":519.1,"input_tokens":5083